      "category": "Grammar & Function Words",
      "target": "です",
      "pronunciation": "desu",
      "audio": "4f82eb288c9c359c.mp3",
      "altAudio": "36c7185f86fcf0b4.mp3",
      "note": "Suffix — attaches to the end of a noun to mean 'is/am/are' (written 〜です (desu) in the source). Example: (わたしは) スミスです。 (Watashi wa Sumisu desu.) — '[I am] Smith.' Attaches directly after the noun with no space, and simply states what someone or something is.",
